  This is a partial chapter, not a claim that all marked estimates or UV
  bounds are complete. Own file chapters/11-marked-insertions.tex. No
  master/preamble edits; no global compilation.

  <section|Proved pieces and sources><label|proved-pieces-and-sources>

  <\enumerate>
    <item>Squarefree source algebra and finite cumulants. Original literature
    checked via publisher: Leonov\UShiryaev1959, Theory Probab
    Appl4(3),319\U329, DOI10.1137/1104031. Entry in
    audit/marked-bibliography.bib. Gaussian pairing cites existing
    Isserlis1918.

    <item>Exact whole-density push, integral invariance under a different
    positive normalized kernel sequence, and field-independent polynomial
    correction. Trish E-Gaussian-sources.tex, lem:E-course-mass. Coefficients
    are L1; Fubini and finite linear algebra prove claims without any
    Markov-law identification between histories.

    <item>Joint terminal large-field terms: Trish E-several-mark.tex,
    lem:E-joint-terminal. Product includes each original activity once and
    retains index/eligibility data; no division by possibly-zero activities.
    Uniform norm bound conditional on weighted local-section complementary
    amplitudes.

    <item>Principal full-support geometry and source-weight change: Martin
    allarity-marked-propagation.tex1\U110 and lem:allarity-weight-raise1958.
    Spare support exponent and multi-cell cover lower bound explicit; neither
    follows from a weaker norm.

    <item>Joint guarded Gaussian comparison: same file
    lem:allarity-guarded-gaussian1266\U1386. Proof reproduced in concise form
    as source-specific common-law estimate using standard moments/Wick. One
    common centered array per mixture member, same mixture for every subset
    and empty term, no independent guards, polynomial invariant under its own
    local rotation. Reference covariance may be symmetric pairing array
    without positivity; actual covariances must be genuine.

    <item>Restart numerical bookkeeping: restarted-rank-history endpoint and
    actual-closure as independently audited in restart-supplier-check.md. Two
    distinct monitor functions/thresholds/radii stated. Clip arithmetic,
    coupling-band match, and short recurrence checked. No inference that
    these scalar inequalities prove analytic closure.

    <item>Corrected entire source Jq_N maps to Jq_k, constant coefficient1.
    No replacement by singleton product.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Exact remaining deliverables><label|exact-remaining-deliverables>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Actual one-insertion coefficient/remainder propagation, invertible
    normalization mathsf Z, estimates on inverse and physical unit.

    <item>Stronger-support full higher-mode bounds on original and restarted
    history. Candidate allarity-marked-propagation2063ff,
    selected-opening2615 and selected-application2704; trace-firesky-gallery
    original-marked-payment/endpoint budget.

    <item>Actual common Gaussian/reader/guard law:
    actual-reader-guarded-curvature, actual-reader-tree-covariance,
    actual-reader-short-covariance, actual-reader-small-window-bridge,
    actual-reader-dawn-selection. Ch6 local estimates alone do not identify
    all cross-entries and marked coordinate maps.

    <item>Same scalar/no duplicated normalization:
    actual-corrected-body-compiler loading/density, gaussian-reassembly,
    actual-mixed-marked-compiler.

    <item>Centered replicated/root bound, original partition normalization
    including harmonic four-power factor; positional modulus.

    <item>Finite-detector absorption and normalized differences:
    fullmesh-fixedbounds-producer, actual-equation-kernel-relay,
    actual-insertion-derivative-relay. Earlier audit checks final algebra but
    not all primitive supplies.

    <item>Volume-uniform correlation derivative theorem and finite-cutoff
    rank statements remain unwritten. No continuum consequence inferred.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Validation><label|validation>

  LaTeX environment balance checked. Initial unresolved chapter8 reference
  corrected to ch08:chapter. New citation sidecar provided. Partial chapter
  explicitly labels remaining work in prose.

  Added finite-dimensional detector section: uniformly bounded equivariant
  projections from invariant inner product; perturbation stability of
  injective free detector; absorption \|Pi x\|\<less\>=2ZC+1 under explicit
  normalized equation comparison; exact finite-difference telescoping.
  Sources restart-supplier-check sections7\U8 and
  fullmesh-fixedbounds-producer. Actual uniform detector/positional/equation
  hypotheses remain explicit, so no circular derivative estimate or continuum
  rank argument is used.

  <section|Continued actual supplier work><label|continued-actual-supplier-work>

  The initial partial-status list above is historical. Current exports:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>ch11:marked-step: three-family actual common-law connected integral
    with explicit inflations, inventory restriction, full support transfer,
    site/incidence bounds. Sources actual-mixed-marked-compiler1\U245 and
    actual corrected body/reassembly. No-body component has no background
    inventory, so purely principal component is genuinely under the common
    probability law.

    <item>ch11:one-graph: exact raw coefficient/remainder estimates, inverse
    and invariant graph ball, delta=C_d epsilon s_f and4delta s_f\<less\>=1,
    fixed-input continuity. Source Trish E-one-mark, plus Martin
    heading-history-handoff216\U331. Reviewer corrections incorporated:
    incoming forced mass m/kappa_f, outgoing remainder measured with
    kappa_c^-1; physical real/imaginary input cost2m.
    Derivative/kernel/period premises, extra fixed-primary derivative, and
    screened polynomial-moment implication now explicit. Source
    polynomial-moment-attenuation1\U130 supplies fixed centered lift/gauge
    germ and filtration proof. Large-support attenuation includes polynomial
    Gaussian scale E_L(beta)exp(-B/2). Continuity is weighted l1 canonical
    path convergence with strict width reserve, and same-norm incoming
    activity convergence, via finite truncation.

    <item>ch11:higher-modes: old higher-mode damping after reweighting, not
    singleton-only induction. Separated cover Br\<less\>=64c_B, two coarse
    reserve units, sufficient fine sigma_f\<minus\>4
    conversion10<ym-middot>15^4(e+9)\<less\>=L(sigma_f\<minus\>4), output
    H_c\<less\>=C_e(exp(-B/64)H_f+zeta). Source Trish E-cover plus Martin
    stronger-support mixed construction. All incidence and forced inventories
    retained.

    <item>ch11:tree-covariance: exact forest curvature covariance
    P_f\<minus\>J P_c J*, with full cross-entries and gauge/harmonic range
    equations. J=H0f^-1 T H0c uses unmodified diagonal operators; actual
    repaired metrics define K,K' and agree on curls. Source
    actual-reader-tree-covariance full, independently checked algebra.

    <item>ch11:actual-reader: same-law actual mean/covariance from6 plus
    curvature Taylor, R=x^-3/8 and normalized O(x^-1/4) error, actual mask
    probability. Produces epsilon=x^-1/32 for fixed finite cleared read
    families. No subset-specific Gaussian samples.

    <item>ch11:replicated: complete coefficient norm and positive denominator
    give exp(Vq+n(x+y+2))/productweights, then exact cell root. Source
    centered-construction80\U115. Vacuum action cost remains explicit; no
    signed activity discarded.

    <item>ch11:positional: independent coordinate-separated Lipschitz modulus
    by transfer trace, Schatten Holder, complex gap Cauchy estimate, common
    quadrature for continuous slice kernels. Original reflection/chessboard
    references verified, Tropp2022Theorem6.32 verified primary lecture notes
    and sidecar added. Source centered-estimates410\U450.

    <item>ch11:trial-descent: inhomogeneous primary subtraction, bank
    inequalities and exp(-(tau_N\<minus\>tau_i)/8) residual; explicit
    terminal protected trial charge E with support exponent/reserve; root
    error C E exp(-tau_N/8), subpower inverse-terminal coordinates. Source
    actual-marked-portfolio-calibration113\U245 and
    actual-insertion-derivative-relay terminal split/descent. Numerical stage
    requirements remain explicit (including e^(81sigma_N), inverse reserve
    subpower, derivative shift2^(varpi q)\<less\>=beta_hat).
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Precise remaining foundational
  dependency><label|precise-remaining-foundational-dependency>

  Chapter2 currently ends without the dressed microscopic equation section.
  Its ordinary local-section theorem is insufficient. Martin
  marked-campaign-producer is the actual source; actual-equation-kernel-relay
  assumes fixed section V_d and invertible regrading R_d with exact
  finite-cutoff null identity on R_d I_d, against all bounded distant
  spectators. Need construct that section and then near-identity same-section
  calibration columns. Thus the actual detector/equation absorption cannot
  yet be advertised as fully discharged, and11 intentionally does not assert
  the all-period finite-difference theorem. This is a specific missing
  monograph construction, not a claim of a global gap in supplied sources.

  No global compilation. Parent handles integration.

  <section|Uniform moving-plane detector and finite differences (latest
  continuation)><label|uniform-moving-plane-detector-and-finite-differences-latest-continuation>

  Added Section ch11:uniform-differences with:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>ch11:uniform-sweep: exact microscopic null identity kills the
    entire replicated comparison, not only its correlation with a fixed
    spectator. Actual calibrated kernel rows with uniform subpower inverse
    coordinates therefore have root norm tending to zero uniformly in all p.

    <item>ch11:uniform-detector: projected free comparison columns span the
    actual moving complement because its dimension equals the free quotient
    dimension at EVERY finite cutoff. No convergence of equation planes is
    used.

    <item>averaged detector assays telescope arbitrary fixed difference
    words, using only the already available primary positional modulus.

    <item>ch11:all-period-differences: absorption bounds the projected
    encoded coefficient; the unnormalized kernel residual is then swept out;
    distinct-cell two-scale packing yields all-period separated difference
    bounds.
  </itemize-minus>

  The theorem retains ONE explicit analytic Assumption
  ch11:finite-detector-input. It is not falsely marked discharged. Source
  fullmesh-fixedbounds-producer366\U490 proves the linear-algebra/averaging
  bridge but imports the actual finite-cutoff matrix estimate from
  actual-rank-purchases. We read actual-rank-purchases1\U320 in full: its
  common-readout contract, exact simultaneous lift equations, cutoff-uniform
  fixed-k bound B_k, corrected-subset root bound, and finite-cell estimate
  are appropriate suppliers. Its own local compiler hypotheses are explicit.

  Concrete remaining estimate: at one sufficiently deep fixed k, on the SAME
  actual restarted window and common readout T, the original-partition
  replicated coefficients for I={1},{2},{1,2}, after free connected
  subtraction, must obey omega^(q\|I\|) \|E replicated coefficient\|
  \<less\>= exp(q I_k), omega=H_k^(1/16)=exp(2 I_k), I_k=log H_k/32. This
  yields root error \<less\>=exp(-I_k), with uniform all-p threshold. Bounded
  same-T lifts solve S_(g_k/t_k)T u_j=W_rho v_j. The fixed-k norm bound
  follows directly from relative readout error\<less\>=1/2 and
  inverse-coordinate bound D_k; that algebra is written.

  Inspected repair chain beyond the high-level statement:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>actual-covariance-fourier-window begins from original uniformly
    elliptic H(0)=I, establishes singular multiplier orders.

    <item>actual-covariance-transport123\U200 gives closed actual mean and
    normal-ordered covariance, with diagonal -B, origin weighted error H^-3
    and full bound H^(lambda/4); these are same atlas data, not an
    independently chosen positive covariance.

    <item>allarity-coordinate-calibration1\U210 constructs exact finite
    coordinate pullback with residual coordinates. Wick covariance may be
    indefinite after normal ordering.

    <item>marked-healthy-cumulant-launch1\U110 constructs closed same-field
    cochain and proves actual-vs-atlas polynomial telescope m epsilon A_D^m.

    <item>allarity-marked-propagation205\U385 gives upper recurrence, exact
    mask reassignment and weighted estimates; late paragraphs2725\U2810
    identify SAME principal guarded moments, common readout, spare support
    run, weight restoration, and complete marked-density identity.

    <item>actual-local-compiler-handoff295\U390 explicitly retains incoming
    neutral-law and genuine small-remainder hypotheses; its selected-course
    closing paragraph requires the matching interval, representation, tube
    and bounds, not mere public-run identity.

    <item>rank-root-normalization160\U275 proves denominator ratio with four
    harmonic-link correction 2 dim(g)log beta/q and large marker weight. This
    is stronger than merely quoting Chapter11's elementary partition lower
    bound.
  </itemize-minus>

  No global gap inferred: supplied Martin repairs plausibly contain the full
  supplier. The monograph still needs their multiscale weighted estimate
  reconstructed and matched to current Chapter6/11 conventions. Current
  one-step actual-reader estimate, higher-mode\<less\>=1, and continuity do
  not alone imply this stronger weighted smallness. Ch14 likewise leaves its
  common grid estimate explicit, so cannot be used circularly.

  <section|Reconstruction of the finite-detector supplier (subsequent
  work)><label|reconstruction-of-the-finite-detector-supplier-subsequent-work>

  The prior paragraph saying the entire comparison remained unwritten is
  superseded by the following additions:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>ch11:common-extraction reconstructs actual-rank-purchases' common
    polynomial map and relative half-error extraction T. It retains the
    actual masked insertion, Taylor approximates near supports only, keeps
    distant/forced factors, uses raw W and positive Wick transform with the
    matching diagonal covariance subtraction, checks adjoint-colour frame
    membership, and solves all columns with this one T.

    <item>ch11:window-covariance reconstructs original-pulse ellipticity
    -\<gtr\> order-zero curvature multiplier with order-one Maxwell error,
    finite-period quadrature at zero, exact response difference quotient,
    cumulative row bound, conditional covariance telescoping, common closed
    coarse field, and one enlarged jet/residual coordinate system.

    <item>ch11:corrected-pair-comparison reconstructs the finite-degree Wick
    estimate and small corrected cumulants, original higher modes' endpoint
    change of weights, exact joint endpoint marked fusion, leading/lower
    counts, and the rank Gaussian numerator/denominator powers.

    <item>ch11:weight-restoration proves regular and forced changes from
    omega_-=H^(1/16\<minus\>U) to omega=H^(1/16), using the SAME coefficients
    at stronger support exponent e+2. Prescribed supports have cover
    \<less\>=C(1+A)^4, so R_e is a finite stage constant; entry delays make
    these and L^4T_e,C_* collectively H^o(1). Reviewer checked cover/fusion
    algebra.

    <item>Weighted compiler estimates now use coupling-dependent
    l\<less\>=H^(q\<minus\>3), m\<less\>=G(x)^\<minus\>2, not the
    insufficient fixed-m statement. Inventory decay is split into explicit
    reserved fractions; subpower l preserves primitive negative coupling
    powers.
  </itemize-minus>

  Precise opening inequality retained: r^m exp((e*+2)c_B(X^+8)) \<less\>=
  H^(\<minus\>q\<minus\>10) r0^m exp(theta0 c_C(X)),
  C=ceil(log\<twosuperior\>s), B=C\<twosuperior\>, r0=s^(\<minus\>a/2),
  r=H^f\<less\>=1. Requires separation \<gtr\>=C\<twosuperior\> for distinct
  marked sites; chosen compact generic configurations have distance
  \<gtr\>=cH^b and satisfy this on the same chart. This is the missing
  comparison between an original polynomially tiny marker radius and the
  larger H-power radius. It is not justified merely by omega_-\<less\>=1.

  Choice-order correction: kappa=1+2(b+2)log(alpha+2)/log3 works for EVERY
  L\<gtr\>=3, so choose kappa,q before Taylor order D and then choose L after
  the polynomial transport norm. No q\<leftrightarrow\>D\<leftrightarrow\>L
  cycle is introduced.

  The actual restarted endpoint/family fragment is being written
  independently by foundations under parent assignment, exporting
  ch11:restart-endpoint/ch11:restart-family/ch11:restart-density. The new
  main-chapter proof invokes that exact interface. Once integrated and
  independently reviewed, the formerly explicit finite-detector input has the
  constructed supplier; keep it visibly as a criterion until the join is
  checked. No new continuum theorem is inferred here.

  <section|Supplier assembled with actual restarted
  family><label|supplier-assembled-with-actual-restarted-family>

  After the independent restarted-history fragment was supplied,
  ch11:finite-detector-input was changed from an assumption to a proposition
  with its reconstruction preceding it. It invokes ch11:restart-family rather
  than assuming a second auxiliary run. The ensuing uniform detector and
  finite-difference theorem now use that proposition.

  Review corrections incorporated:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Exact local split uses f_near,mask only, not the full insertion;
    distant regular and original forced terms remain separate.

    <item>Rescaled polynomial p_u=W_u((theta/g)y) has coefficient bound
    \<less\>=H^alpha \|\|Au\|\| and radial rows \<less\>=H^alpha before the
    Wick estimate.

    <item>Actual solved-lift amplification is H^(bd+c_d), retained in initial
    singleton remainder powers; c_d is independent of b.

    <item>Zero extension of the local closed background is accompanied by the
    omitted response-path error CB^a exp(-cB)g^{-1}; it is not claimed to
    preserve a global conditional mean exactly.

    <item>The denominator estimate contains an explicit axial priority order
    selecting 3V\<minus\>3 plaquettes, and the four remaining wrapping links
    account for the harmonic correction.

    <item>Bounded prescribed-support charge R_f applies to nonzero connected
    principal components and at middle/restoration levels. The widely
    separated opening marks use the separate connected-cover suppression
    estimate.

    <item>Fixed stage factors R_f,C_*,L^4T_e and incidence constants are
    collectively delayed to H^o(1), rather than silently regarded as uniform
    constants across stages.
  </itemize-minus>

  The reconstruction is now subject to independent mathematical review by
  foundations and continuum agents. No global build was run by this agent.

  <section|Finite-arity and finite-menu export><label|finite-arity-and-finite-menu-export>

  Added ch11:n-mark-comparison with root bound ch11:n-mark-root: for any
  fixed n, all nonempty coefficients of the actual source divided by the free
  subset-moment polynomial have root \<less\>=H^(-1/(16n)). Use
  omega=H^(1/(8n)), log-normalizer I=logH/(16n); moment comparison uses
  degree nD and lambda\<less\>=1/(32 n\<twosuperior\>(D+1)), then finite
  connected logarithm on a bounded neighborhood of free subset moments.
  Upper/restoration/lower estimates already carry explicit n and2^n and
  therefore extend without an unbounded-arity claim.

  One actual coefficient extraction T per degree is used for any fixed finite
  list of magnifications. Choose D and requests jointly and restart once on
  the longest window; shorter windows are restrictions, not separately
  normalized histories. Signed equivariance is obtained by averaging the raw
  polynomial construction BEFORE defining T, with stricter pre-average
  relative error. Exact dilation relations between different
  own-normalization lifts give the size/displacement amplification
  H^((b0\<minus\>bj)d). No claim that one fixed raw label has small corrected
  error at all magnifications.

  Uniformity uses full point separation, not coordinatewise separation.
  Comparison-cell side \<less\>=a_kH^(b+5) follows from upper ratio\<less\>=L
  H^(b+2), lower ratio\<less\>=L C^10 and stage delay
  L\<twosuperior\>C^10\<less\>=H\<threesuperior\>.

  Reviewed parent's unintegrated14-lattice-comparison.tex against this
  export: reciprocal recursion, fixed-n exponent, finite-menu same-T
  compatibility and own-normalization singleton amplification match.
</body>

